WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:10.000
Culture of Jeju Haenyeo — Women Divers
Jeju Island, South Korea

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:22.000
[Women divers who harvest seafood 10 meters
below the surface — without oxygen tanks]

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:35.000
[Holding their breath for one minute per dive,
they work up to seven hours a day, 90 days a year]

4
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:47.000
[Divers are ranked by experience — hagun, junggun,
and sanggun — with elders guiding the young]

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:58.000
[In the 1960s, 23,000 haenyeo worked these waters.
Today, only 4,000 remain — most over sixty]

6
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:08.000
[Their distinctive whistle upon resurfacing —
the sumbisori — is the sound of survival itself]

7
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:16.000
[UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage since 2016 —
a tradition sustained by breath, skill, and the sea]
